arbon Reduction Plan has been completed in accordance with PPN 06/21 and associated\nguidance and reporting standard for Carbon Reduction Plans. Emissions have been reported and\nrecorded in accordance with the published reporting standard for Carbon Reduction Plans and the\nGHG Reporting Protocol corporate standard and uses the appropriate Government emission\nconversion factors for greenhouse gas company reporting.\nScope 1 and Scope 2 emissions have been reported in accordance with SECR requirements, and the\nrequired subset of Scope 3 emissions have been reported in accordance with the published reporting\nstandard for Carbon Reduction Plans and the Corporate Value Chain (Scope 3) Standard.\nThis Carbon Reduction Plan has been reviewed and signed off by the board of directors (or equivalent\nmanagement body).\nSigned on behalf of the Supplier:\nJohn Speight\nPresident and Head of Europe (EVP)", "heading": "", "source": "Carbon_New_2040.pdf", "title": "Carbon Reduction Plan", "cite": 1, "page_start": 3, "page_end": 3, "norm_start": 6087, "norm_end": 8898, "score": 0.03252247488101534, "confident": false, "derived": false, "ocr": false, "superseded": false, "status": "current", "version_group": null, "superseded_by": null, "supersedes": null, "review_date": null}, {"parent_id": "580173bc3dad048d", "text": "Carbon Reduction Plan\nSupplier name: Coforge Limited & All International Locations (including Coforge U.K Limited)\nPublication date: 10 October 2025\nCommitment to Achieving Net Zero\nCoforge Limited and other Global Business Operations, including Coforge U.K. Limited are committed\nto achieve Net Zero emission by 2040. Coforge U.K. Limited is a wholly owned subsidiary of Coforge\nLimited.\nBaseline Emissions Footprint\nBaseline emissions are a record of the greenhouse gases that have been produced in the past and\nwere produced prior to the introduction of any strategies to reduce emissions. Baseline emissions are\nthe reference point against which emissions reduction can be measured.\n*There is no Scope 1 (Direct) emission in the UK as no offices in these locations use natural gas, oil, LPG or have\nany owned vehicles.", "heading": "", "source": "Carbon_New_2040.pdf", "title": "Carbon Reduction Plan", "cite": 2, "page_start": 1, "page_end": 1, "norm_start": 0, "norm_end": 822, "score": 0.032266458495966696, "confident": false, "derived": false, "ocr": false, "superseded": false, "status": "current", "version_group": null, "superseded_by": null, "supersedes": null, "review_date": null}, {"parent_id": "2a6dc7c86dcd01c0", "text": "Current year emissions: FY25\n*There is no Scope 1 (Direct) related emission in the UK as no offices in these locations use natural gas, oil, LPG\nor have any owned vehicles. Only potential source of emission is backup diesel generators. However, we reported\nno emissions as they have not been used. India has approximately 20,000 people across multiple campuses and\nconstitutes lion’s share of our employees and therefore, is the biggest emissions contributor.\nEmissions Reduction Targets\nCoforge is a fast-growing IT services firm, and the business has grown over 100% in the past 4 years.\nThe growth in the business has led to an increase in headcount and operations across the globe. As an\norganisation, we acknowledge that this could lead to increase in absolute emissions, directly\nproportionate to the increase in headcount and business operations. However, as an organisation, we\nare committed to assessing our carbon emissions and target to have zero carbon emissions by 2040.\nWe aim to achieve our target by taking active steps through carbon sequestration and use of renewable\nenergy technologies, such as solar.\nIndia location – Since FY24, when the baseline emissions were assessed, there has been a\ncontinuous focus on emission reduction and focused interventions to ensure that the scope of\nemissions is controlled despite the growth of our business operations. Several of our pilot carbon\nreduction initiatives were conducted in our India operations.\nInternational locations (including the UK) – In 2022, we conducted emission assessment for all\ninternational business operations, including the UK. We are looking to undertake multiple initiatives to\ncontrol these emissions, such as reducing the need for air-travel where possible, given that it is a\nsignificant contributor to our emissions for international locations. We are continually assessing our\noperations for consolidation of resources to reduce the negative impact on the environment.\nCarbon Reduction Initiatives\nIn alignment with our goal to be “net-zero by 2040”, we have undertaken the following initiatives and\nare actively integrating carbon reduction plans in our global operations:\n1. Coforge has obtained certain global certifications that allow us to reduce our overall carbon\nemissions across our operations:\n• Environment, Health, and Safety Management System has been implemented in\nconformance to ISO 14001:2015 and ISO 45001:2018 standards.\n• Coforge owns USGBC (US Green Building Council)-rated Platinum green campuses.\n2. We are committed to the utilization of clean fuel and a transition to renewable energy in our\noperations. This covers a wide variety of our operations, including transportation, cafeteria\noperations and electricity consumption.\n• 100% conversion of company cabs and buses to Compressed Natural Gas (CNG).\n• Introduce electric vehicle fleets (for employees’ transport system) and target 10%\nintegration by 2028 and ~50% by 2032.\n• 100% utilization of Piped Natural Gas (PNG) in cafeteria operations.\n• Procure 10% green energy, contributing to total energy consumption by 2025 and\nachieve ~ 50% by 2030.\n• Support transition to 100% renewable energy by 2040 by committing to the RE100\nglobal initiative. Through this, we pledge to have 100% of our electricity sourced from\nrenewable sources.", "heading": "", "source": "Carbon_New_2040.pdf", "title": "Carbon Reduction Plan", "cite": 3, "page_start": 2, "page_end": 2, "norm_start": 2432, "norm_end": 5737, "score": 0.03200204813108039, "confident": false, "derived": false, "ocr": false, "superseded": false, "status": "current", "version_group": null, "superseded_by": null, "supersedes": null, "review_date": null}, {"parent_id": "638ee6f65ae26b8e", "text": "recycle, and reuse) especially for food, plastic, and other recyclable/ bio-degradable waste to minimize waste\nto landfill.\n• Drive responsible management of water through conservation, harvesting, and recycling of wastewater,\nrespectively for reducing consumption of fresh water and reusing of recycled water within the premises.\n• Environmental awareness training and education for our employees, alongside effective communication with\nemployees and recognition of their initiatives and achievements towards environmental improvement.\n• Undertake independent environmental auditing, verification, and certification of our operations, practices and\nalong our supply chain, as applicable.\n• Integration of ESG/Sustainability compliances and parameters as part of registration, onboarding, review, and\nsupplier development processes for all major suppliers as applicable. Periodic vendor/supplier assessment for\nthe identified critical suppliers will be conducted covering aspects related to environmental and social\ncompliances and performance.\n• Drive capacity building sessions for our vendors/suppliers to motivate them to adopt environment\nsustainability practices and social responsibility in their business strategy and operations, in accordance with\nCoforge’s Vendor Code of Conduct.\nThis Policy clearly defines Coforge’s commitments to carbon neutrality, waste management and water conservation,\nand the incorporation of sustainable practices into our overall business operations. These commitments are managed\nthrough set environmental sustainability targets that are applicable across our company.\nEnergy Optimization and Emission Management\nWe, at Coforge, are committed to become “Carbon Neutral in our operations by 2040”. In line with this commitment,\nwe have established a sub-target of continuous reduction of GHG emissions by 5% year-on-year, through adoption of\nenergy efficient technologies/solutions, optimization of energy usage, increase share of renewable energy to total\nenergy, and biodiversity conservation initiatives that have a cascading effect on carbon offsets.\nWe are making steady progress against our goal of reducing carbon emissions through an integrated approach. Some\nof our internal commitments are mentioned below:\n• Procure 10% of electricity from green sources by 2025 and increase the share to ~50% by 2030. Transition\nto 100% renewable energy by 2050 by committing to the RE100 initiative.\n• Increase share of electric vehicles (EVs) in fleet for employee commute to 10% by 2025 and to 50% by 2040.\nAt Coforge, we conduct annual checks on our equipment and optimize operational processes to minimize energy\nwastage and optimize energy efficiency. To increase employee awareness, we conduct one mandatory and two\nvoluntary training sessions annually, empowering them with adequate knowledge and skills on energy-saving\npractices and emission management strategies.\nWaste Management and Circularity\nCoforge has committed to become “Zero Waste by 2040” by creating an effective waste management ecosystem by\nadopting the following sub-targets:\n• The ‘Zero Food Waste’ commitment at Coforge is achieved through diversion of food waste to composting\npractices and feed to livestock to minimize waste to landfill.\n• The ‘Zero Plastic Waste’ commitment at Coforge is reinforced by eliminating the use of single-use plastic on\nour premises and responsible disposal of plastics as per local laws and mandates, i.e., through authorized\nvendors.\n• The ‘Zero Waste to Landfill’ initiative at Coforge is supported by our Scrap/E-Waste Disposal Policy,\nresponsible and scientific disposal of hazardous waste generated and proper recycling of non-food waste\nthrough authorized recycler vendors.", "heading": "", "source": "Envi_2040-1.pdf", "title": "Sustainability Policy", "cite": 4, "page_start": 1, "page_end": 7, "norm_start": 4269, "norm_end": 7992, "score": 0.030776515151515152, "confident": false, "derived": false, "ocr": false, "superseded": false, "status": "current", "version_group": "vg_envi20401_environmentalsustainabil", "superseded_by": null, "supersedes": "Environmental_Sustainability_Policy_2025.pdf", "review_date": "2026-03-10"}, {"parent_id": "ec15ac08c49e6cd1", "text": "Environmental\nSustainability Policy\nReview Date – 10th March 2026\nLast Review – 1st April 2025\nContents\nScope ......................................................................................................................... 3\nPurpose ........................................................................................................................ 3\nPolicy commitment ........................................................................................................ 3\nEnergy Optimization and Emission Management .............................................................. 4\nWaste Management and Circularity ................................................................................. 4\nWater Management ....................................................................................................... 5\nEnvironmental Management System ............................................................................... 5\nClimate Change Adaptation ............................................................................................ 5\nDecarbonization Strategy ............................................................................................... 5\nMonitoring .................................................................................................................... 5\nCompliance Obligations .................................................................................................. 6\nScope\nTo foster sustainable business development, Coforge is committed to incorporate environmentally conscious practices\namongst all its employees, extended workforce as well as along the supply chain, to whatever extent possible.\nThis Policy will remain applicable to all facilities and locations of Coforge (rented/ leased or owned) and the\nemployees and other stakeholders associated with them.\nCoforge will also extend the applicability of this Policy across the value chain, to whatever extent possible. All thirdparty associates of Coforge, including suppliers, contractors, vendors, and affiliates, are expected and encouraged to\ncomply to this Policy.\nPurpose\nCoforge Limited (hereafter referred to as “Coforge”) is a global digital services and business solutions provider with\nin-depth domain expertise that specializes in selected industry verticals. The company strategy is rooted in providing\ncapability at scale with focus on emerging technologies, building partnerships, focusing on client centricity, and\ncreating a sustainable and responsible world. Acknowledging its impact and footprint on environment and natural\nresources, the company has developed its ‘Environmental Sustainability Policy’ to address the pressing issues of\nClimate Change and Environmental Management for Coforge and its value chain. The policy aims to build trust with\nstakeholders, increase operational efficiency, and ensure that all its services are environmentally sound and rendered\nin responsible manner.\nPolicy commitment\nAt Coforge, we recognize the criticality of being a responsible business and believe in creating value for its\nemployees, extended workforce, shareholders, investors, vendors, suppliers, customers, and other stakeholders.\nBeing a responsible company, it is a prerequisite to comply with all applicable legal requirements, but being a\nresponsible and sustainable company, it is imperative to embed the principles of sustainable development in\ncompany’s core business strategy, operational activities and services offered. Coforge is therefore committed to the\nfollowing:\n• Ensure 100% compliance with all applicable legal and regulatory requirements of the laws of the land,\nwherever it operates in.\n• Establish, track, and monitor environmental goals and targets to ensure compliance and performance of the\ncompany with timelines.\n• Disclose accurate and adequate environmental information based on scientific evidence and data trails for\nstakeholder review of company’s performance.\n• Reduce Coforge’s Greenhouse Gas (GHG) emissions and carbon footprint generated from business operations\nby adopting energy efficient technologies and moving towards renewable energy sources, as applicable.\n• Implement sustainable waste management practices, based on principle of circularity, i.e., 3Rs (reduce,\nrecycle, and reuse) especially for food, plastic, and other recyclable/ bio-degradable waste to minimize waste\nto landfill.\n• Drive responsible management of water through conservation, harvesting, and recycling of wastewater,\nrespectively for reducing consumption of fresh water and reusing of recycled water within the premises.\n• Environmental awareness training and education for our employees, alongside effective communication with\nemployees and recognition of their initiatives and achievements towards environmental improvement.\n• Undertake independent environmental auditing, verification, and certification of our operations, practices and", "heading": "", "source": "Envi_2040-1.pdf", "title": "Sustainability Policy", "cite": 5, "page_start": 1, "page_end": 7, "norm_start": 0, "norm_end": 4918, "score": 0.03055037313432836, "confident": false, "derived": false, "ocr": false, "superseded": false, "status": "current", "version_group": "vg_envi20401_environmentalsustainabil", "superseded_by": null, "supersedes": "Environmental_Sustainability_Policy_2025.pdf", "review_date": "2026-03-10"}], "reason": "", "mode": "rrf", "retrieve_ms": 766, "stages_ms": {"embed": 755.7105839950964, "dense": 3.3173339907079935, "lexical": 0.8137090044328943, "fuse": 0.17262499022763222, "gate": 0.3028750070370734, "total": 764.4146259990521}, "cached": false, "request_id": "01a0cbb3-66cc-73dc-a9af-d1dc59fd0613", "trace_id": "01a0cbb3-66cc-73dc-a9af-d1dc59fd0613", "degraded": [], "index_generation": 4, "verification": {"state": "withheld", "reason": "missing_citation", "unsupported": []}, "gated": true}

